{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/57766-a-hedgespinning-snag","id":57766,"title":"A Hedgespinning Snag","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-25T17:18:42-08:00","id":57766,"title":"A Hedgespinning Snag","content":"I have a character with a decent Craft pool and he is interested in hedgespinning. After plumbing the rules and various online sources, my ST has agreed to use this site as a base line:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://thereachmux.org/wiki/Changeling/Hedgespinning#Zero_Dot_Trinkets\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://thereachmux.org/wiki/Changeling/Hedgespinning#Zero_Dot_Trinkets\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://thereachmux.org/wiki/Changeling/Hedgespinning#Zero_Dot_Trinkets\" target=\"_blank\"> http://thereachmux.org/wiki/Changeling/Hedgespinning#Zero_Dot_Trinkets </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I\u2019m generally happy with the mechanics, except for \u201cZero Dot Trinkets\u201d. As my character is just starting he is not likely to have many extra XP for fancy items and on a story level he would like to start with a couple of small items to prove he can do it at all. Plus, I like the idea that my character could have fancy clothes when dealing with other fae, but have it look plain and indistinct to mortals.<br /> <br /> My conundrum: the site we are using says success target for creation is X3 of item dots. So, a 0dot item is free? That does not seem fair, especially because each garment will still be a +1 to changeling social pools.<br /> <br /> How would you suggest handling this issue specifically? Also, does your group handle hedgespinning in some other way that might be smoother or more fun?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T17:38:56-08:00","id":57775,"title":"","content":"Every token or hedgespun trinket has a story linked to its creation, even low level ones. From a certain mechanics standpoint, it looks like a pretty easy way to trick out your character with persistent, passive bonuses to one's dice pool. However, the process of hedgespinning is not just rolling your Crafts dicepool and spending some XP. The various &quot;ingredients&quot; and materials that goes into making hedgespun should represent a story in and of itself, which itself offers up various challenges and risks. Sure, the 0-Dot Hedgespun cloak woven from cocoon silk and tomorrow's regrets may not cost any XP as part of the dice rolling to make the cloak itself ... but the person who made it had to gather the silk from the larva of black winged cadaver moths (which can only be found in the mouth of a corpse of a man killed due to vengeance) and spin it into thread spun in the presence of young women waiting in the local planned parenthood. <br /> <br /> There is still an investment, it's just not XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T18:58:39-08:00","id":57821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/57766-a-hedgespinning-snag?p=57775#post57775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every token or hedgespun trinket has a story linked to its creation, even low level ones. From a certain mechanics standpoint, it looks like a pretty easy way to trick out your character with persistent, passive bonuses to one's dice pool. However, the process of hedgespinning is not just rolling your Crafts dicepool and spending some XP. The various &quot;ingredients&quot; and materials that goes into making hedgespun should represent a story in and of itself, which itself offers up various challenges and risks. Sure, the 0-Dot Hedgespun cloak woven from cocoon silk and tomorrow's regrets may not cost any XP as part of the dice rolling to make the cloak itself ... but the person who made it had to gather the silk from the larva of black winged cadaver moths (which can only be found in the mouth of a corpse of a man killed due to vengeance) and spin it into thread spun in the presence of young women waiting in the local planned parenthood.<br /> <br /> There is still an investment, it's just not XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I accept all of that as par for the course. Does that mean you think no roll is needed for a Zero dot item? I get that the story is paramont, but the game has mechanics for a reason (theoretically) and if that is true, what is a fair target siccess total for my PCs ultimate craft roll to verify that I did tyrn that hard won silk into an 0dot item of my desire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T20:01:29-08:00","id":57846,"title":"","content":"Would your ST care if your character had a gun, and it made sense for your characters background?<br /> Frankly, I would be shocked if you said no.<br /> <br /> so you want some hedge spun contraptions and clothes; clothes are a situation social bonus and contraptions are the Fae equivalent normal objects.<br /> if you really need to roll for a &quot;zero dot&quot; item build in game I would say that a single roll taking up to an hour depending on the materials and complexity, success means you made it failure means you didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T05:55:45-08:00","id":58045,"title":"","content":"Okay, Basketcase, I see the 1 simple success option, but let me extrapolate on that. Assume my PC finds in teh hedge a giant spider web and deals with the spider, then takes all the wonderful web silk. the web was huge plenty to make a belt,slippers, hat, cloves and a tie. Now my PC haas a craft of three, Int 3 and access to the correct tools in a workshop. So, statistically I am extreemly likely to gain one success with every roll. You are saying that for one short 5 hour day in my workshop, I am justified in recieving a total +5 on all Cgangeling social rolls?<br /> I certainly like that version, it very much swings the game in my favor. Does everyone else get that kind of leeway with their stuff? Is it just that we don't think socializing matters as much as fighting--take all the social pluses you want, but pay out the wazzoo for a little extra damage or armor?<br /> I am asking because I want to get as much as I can for my PC with the rules allowed, but I don't want to unbalance the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T12:16:58-08:00","id":58238,"title":"","content":"GitariArt I would stop you at +3 taking about a full days work. I just don't believe any amount or quality of clothing should be worth +5, unless it is specifically magical.<br /> <br /> Socializing matters just as much as combat (my personal opinion). And like combat details matter, a nice suit is only helpful around people you respect wealth. Those bonuses could turn to negatives in a biker bar or goblin mine. details like that are what keep social balance. but in the right circumstances; a nice suit +3, flashing lots of cash +2, an entourage +3, reputation +?, title +?. All add up while not unbalancing the game.<br /> <br /> Going this route makes you the face man for the motley, which can be more responsibility then you'd expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T13:01:02-08:00","id":58259,"title":"","content":"Honestly, GitariArt, I think you are approaching this in the wrong way. You craft a &quot;recipe&quot; for each Hedgespun item you make, and the list of ingredients is specific towards that single piece of Hedgespun. It shouldn't be generic. So, let's say that you find the giant spider's web and harvest the silk. It isn't like you can then just take the material and then just craft a bunch of things in an hour that gives you +1 to all your Social rolls. It isn't like that. It is all about intent and the narrative elements of the Hedgespun that determines the path of its creation. To continue along the lines of your example, your changeling will find the spider's web and be inspired to make something out of it. That web is considered one ingredient in a recipe for a single hedgespun garment and ideally whatever it is that you are making will have some sort of symbolic connection with spiders and webs, if only metaphorically. The recipe is something you come up with or you have found, but it is never something mundane. Even 0 Dot tokens are narratively important in some way.<br /> <br /> As for having your character bedecked in Hedgespun, hoping that you can get ludicrous bonuses to your rolls, remember that those bonuses should be specific to certain Social rolls with other fairies. Your hedgespun necktie may give +1 bonus to Politics when dealing other fairies, but that die modifier doesn't stack with the +1 modifier to dancing that your hedgespun slippers grants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T16:18:06-08:00","id":58387,"title":"","content":"Basketcase, I have to say that I am glad you are not my ST. In your first post you said the rules were 1 hr per roll and only one success needed for a 0dot item. In your next post you arbitrarily would stop me at +3 and dictate a different timeline than the rolls needed. I just could not play in a game where I could not rely on my ST be fair and consistent. <br /> As for the nice suit comment, according to the rule books any hedgespun item elicits a +1 to any social rolls when dealing with another changeling, regardless of any other powers or basic appearance of the item.<br /> Firefly Night, I definitely appiciate your reitterating you possitoon, I feel I understant your point much better. Your comments about recipes is solid. Unless I have a resipe for a scarf and choose to just make five of the one type of garment. Again, the rule books say +1 social rolls per item with no mention of having multiple belts, scrafs, etc. Even so, as long as my ST makes such a limitation clear prior to my making the items, I woaccept that they are the final arbiter.<br /> I definitely like the lean towards ingredients/recipe influencing outcome. However, since I am talking about 0dot items--thus no additional powers, beyond the simple +1 social that all hedgespin get--there are no other aspects to influence. I understand that you have decided that the type of social roll should be watered down to a specific skill type. Personally, I just don't see that writen in the rules, while I do see the rules saying any social roll.<br /> To any readers, I am worried that I am sounding blindly argimentative and petulant. In fact, I am very much enjoying what I think of as a spirited theoretical debate. No matter what this is all just opinions. So, I am not trying to win or prove any points, I am just trying to explore the topic as deeply as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T08:36:53-08:00","id":58731,"title":"","content":"Don't worry, man. We are all nerds here ... and nerdery, by its very nature, is a petulant past-time defined by its sophistry and pedantry. No need to apologize. Asking forgiveness from internet nerds is way j-v.<br /> <br /> Continuing.<br /> <br /> I decided to refresh myself on the actual rules for Hedgespinning and Hedgespun Raiment as presented in the <b>Changeling: The Lost</b> core and <b>Rites of Spring</b>. I felt as if something was missing in my understanding of the rules dilemma you are facing and I had already completed my viewing of Downton Abbey. So, first I looked up the rules for Hedgespun Raiment as presented on Pg. 203 of the Core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pg. 203, heading &quot;Hedgespun Raiment O to OOO<br /> <br /> [....] While possessing no actual supernatural power, Hedgespun is something of a Status symbol among the Lost, and many courtiers wouldn't be caught dead at a grand Revel in simple mortal clothing. The one-dot version represents <i><b>an entire outfit of Hedgespun clothing</b></i>; Storytellers are encouraged to allow any character a single, small article of Hedgespun clothing (a bloody red cap, a flame-coloured scarf, a glittering monocle) <i>at no cost</i>. </div> </div> </div>Okay. So, nowhere is there any mention of a dice modifier to a changeling's Social rolls, nor is there an option to buy a zero dot token's worth of Hedgespun. There is a mention of a completely cosmetic application of this Token that the GM is encouraged to give their players as a means to personalize their character. Also, note the section that I bolded; &quot; ... an entire outfit ....&quot; This makes me think that bonuses, if any, should only be applied at a minimum of 1 Dot of this Token and it must constitute the entire look of the changeling's raiment. Thus, no +5 to every Social roll because your outfit consists of Hedgespun shoes, necktie, jacket, hat and gloves. That entire outfit would still just give a +1 &quot;look at me I'm awesome!&quot; modifier with other fairy types.<br /> <br /> Okay, so what about that +1 modifier to all Social rolls. That is a pretty ridiculous bonus, even if you can't cheese it out with over the top fairy accessorizing. There is more stuff about Hedgespun clothes in <b>Rites of Spring</b>, so let us check it out!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rites of Spring, pg. 143<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> Hedgespun Raiment - any kind of clothing or armor spun from elements found amongst the Thorns - can be found on pg. 203 of Changeling: The Lost. Below, however, are few <b>additional</b> ways the Storyteller <b>might</b> allow one to <b>spend dots</b> purchased in the Merit.<br /> <br /> [snip]<br /> <br /> * The Hedgespun raiment might add to other particular Social rolls at a rate of +1 per dot spent. A piece of blood-spattered ivory armor might add to Intimidation by dint of its menacing appearance. A long pelt that gives off a potent and pungent musk might grant the user dice in Animal Ken [...]<br /> </div> </div> </div>And here we get to the heart of the topic. The above passage seems to indicate that a Merit dot must be spent in order to get any sort of dice bonus to a <i>particular</i> use of a Social skill. There is no where in the text that mentions any ability that will give you a flat bonus to *all* applications of such a broad category of Skills at such a cheap (read: free) cost. Hedgespun, RAW, when given as a free cosmetic &quot;mini-token&quot; to players provides no bonuses to any rolls, be they Social or not, unless the GM feels that the item is pertinent enough to the scene to illicit it. Even when merit dots are spent to buy the Hedgespun Raiment, the dice modifier to Social rolls are bought with dots and only apply to a specific skill.<br /> <br /> So, it seems to me that the problem does not rest with those of us who disagree with your game's implementation of Hedgespun. The problem rests with your Storyteller, who most likely misinterpreted the text and does not have the experience to realize that the abilities he is giving to his players are pretty ridiculous. However, if the game is fun and everybody agrees to things, who cares if it is not &quot;canon.&quot; Enjoy it!<br /> <br /> That being said, it is a bit hard for us to comment on the validity of house rules since our only shared point of reference is that actual text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","user":"Firefly Night","date":". 01-27-2014, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T11:31:42-08:00","id":58938,"title":"","content":"The section that GitariArt is referencing about how hedgespun effects social roles is a section from Rites of Spring (p. 144):<br /> <br /> <i>Wondrous Allure<br /> Hedgespun items do not create an actual bump to a changeling\u2019s Status score; other Lost are at least dimly aware that possessing such a token does not give one any kind of magical authority (unless the token literally has that as a power, and some do), any more than owning a Prada bag doesn\u2019t guarantee a step up the social ladder.<br /> <br /> What it does do, however, is boost a changeling\u2019s allure in social situations. For each Hedgespun item visibly present on or near a character (and possessed by the character), that character gains a +1 boost to any Socialize rolls made. Owning a pair of slippers made of iridescent eels and a nose ring hammered out of a goblin\u2019s metal-tipped tooth counts as two visible Hedgespun tokens, and while visible the character gains +2 to Socialize rolls (though this bonus is only applicable among other changelings).<br /> <br /> If she\u2019s hosting a party in her condo and she features a prominent sculpture carved of spiraling Fae bones, that earns her an additional +1 bonus (because who doesn\u2019t want to talk about such a find, and who isn\u2019t impressed that she possesses such a special piece of art?). A Storyteller may decide over time that these bonuses fade; a character who shows off the same pocket watch made of moonglass and moth bits time and time again certainly loses the effect over time. Smart changelings know that such social potency wears down, and squan- dering such wondrous allure is a true waste, indeed. </i><br /> <br /> It's an easy section to miss because it's the very last one, mostly on a page with information about tokens. It does seem to indicate that any hedgespun is pretty cool to other Changelings, and it's not especially dependent on it being a particular type of cool (leather jacket or a silk suit, it's all magically delicious).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2002-quynce","name":"Quynce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2002_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T11:45:03-08:00","id":58950,"title":"","content":"Ugh. Man, what is it with World of Darkness books being so damn contradictory and hard to navigate? Discussing the rules can get as crazy as having a theological debate about the Bible. Changeling is in desperate need of a 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> Anyway: So, the bonus is only to Socialize rolls (as in the skill) and not all Social rolls (the category)... and it is a bonus that is not dependent on any supernatural aspect of said Hedgespun? It is a modifier dependent on the viewer's sense of novelty. Confusing, for sure, but still a lot less potent than having that bonus apply to ALL social rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T12:48:00-08:00","id":59022,"title":"","content":"I'm not crazy!... At least not about that particular game quote. *phew*<br /> Amen, to White Wold's lack of organization. Indexes and Tables of Content just aren't that hard, pretty much any word processor will make them for you. Now if only the publishers would bother to use them.<br /> Anyway...<br /> Since the three primary catagories are Mental, Physical, and Social, I could see &quot;any socialize rolls&quot; as referencing all the skills within that set. However, I also see how that's me grubbing for more, for a character that gets no ten agains in most Social situations. So, I put that issue asside.<br /> I love the idea that the bonus fades over amount of exposure. I feel that it mkes it more balanced. Thus, my PC may show up at a gathering in 5 hedge-scarfs and really wow the assembly, but the next time I try it with someone from that gathering it just starts to seem more and more like a desperate desire for attention. Although, I would suggest that a 1dot item retain allure longer than a 0dot and 2 mor ethan 1, etc.<br /> As far as the mechanics go for actually determining success, I don't think it gets better than basketcase'a suggestion of 1 success for 0dot item, simce the website my ST is basing the house rules on says a 1dot item only needs three successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}